// Pull request: #6615 New: ScreenConnect Client Spawns Script Host / Run Key Set To Launch VBScript
// Pull request URL: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/pull/6615
// Pull request author: Mohammedalkahala
// Change: new rule
// Title: Run Key Set To Launch VBScript Via Script Host
// Sigma ID: 53ab10ca-696a-4c2f-8ba2-1e992a2e2ad6
// Status: experimental | Level: medium
// Author: Mohammed Alkahala
// Date: 2026-11-13 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: persistence, T1547.001, execution, T1059.005
// Description: Detects a "Run" or "RunOnce" registry value being set to launch a VBScript file through a
//   Windows script host. Threat actors use this for persistence, for example a "WindowsServiceHost"
//   Run value pointing to a .vbs file in the user profile, as seen in rogue ScreenConnect
//   intrusions.
// False positives:
//   - Legacy software that starts helper VBScript files at logon. Allow-list these by full path.
// References:
//   - https://www.huntress.com/blog/rogue-screenconnect-installations
//   - https://github.com/Mohammedalkahala/purpleloop/tree/main/detections/huntress-rmm-wsh
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/05c24c8969df151d53ffa681efdc812a61713ca7/rules/windows/registry/registry_set/registry_set_persistence_run_key_vbscript.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language, Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.
// Note: 2 wildcard comparison(s) rewritten to 'matches regex' (KQL treats * in contains/endswith/== as a literal character)

DeviceRegistryEvents
| where (RegistryKey matches regex @"(?i)\\Software\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Run.*$" or RegistryKey matches regex @"(?i)\\Software\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\RunOnce.*$") and (RegistryValueData contains "wscript" or RegistryValueData contains "cscript") and (RegistryValueData contains ".vbs" or RegistryValueData contains ".vbe")
